E2AD                             ; ---- machine code: the grave
E2AD                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
E2AD                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (60h) is
E2AD                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
E2AD                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ); see the
E2AD                             ; contract in the header.
E2AD   20 20 E4     H_GRAVE:   JSR   rdhex   
